  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A few gusty thunderstorms possible this afternoon.\n\nMid level shortwave will move across the Ohio Valley this afternoon. \nBuilding instability during peak heating will support the \ndevelopment of a few showers and thunderstorms with this wave during \nthe afternoon into the evening. The greatest potential for any \nthunderstorms will likely be inland from the stable lakes. Threat \nfor severe weather is low with only marginal instability, but enough \nflow aloft with bulk shear of around 40 knots could produce a few \ngusty thunderstorms.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Summer-like heat Monday and Tuesday.\n\nHeights will rise starting Sunday and continuing into early next \nweek as ridging establishes over the eastern CONUS. This will boost \ntemperatures into the 80s across much of western and north-central \nNew York, with a few lowers 90s possible for some of our normally \nwarmest spots. Some record high temperatures will be within reach, \nbut lower humidity levels will likely keep any heat headlines out of \nthe forecast. Given the building warmth through early next week, its \nworth noting that area water temperatures are still not that warm \nand in the 40s to lower 50s. Take precautions if you plan to visit \nany area waterways this weekend and next week.",
